you do not have to pose.

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's not --"
I go, "I was just taking

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:26.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
a picture of you
in your bedroom.

00:07:26.012 --> 00:07:26.779 line:92%
Just let me take a photo.

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:28.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought your sweater
was cute."

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everything,
she just keeps going...

00:07:30.216 --> 00:07:31.184 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Everything's that.

00:07:31.184 --> 00:07:32.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the other one
gets involved.

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This one's a little loose
with the pose.

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:35.655 line:92%
-Well, she was trying to guess

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:38.324
"Maybe two hands is better
than one with the pose."

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:42.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
But now my kids won't do
anything but pose for photos

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:43.463 line:92%
And I go, "That's not how --

00:07:43.463 --> 00:07:44.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can just take
an actual photo.

00:07:44.797 --> 00:07:45.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't have to
really do this."

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:47.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's the cutest thing.
I'm loving it.

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Be natural like the giraffe
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:53.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right. Yeah, just be natural
exactly, correct.

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:55.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, this is --
We're gonna be right back.

00:07:55.341 --> 00:07:58.511
We're gonna talk about you
fourth -- your fourth book

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:00.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow. Is it though?
[ Both laugh ]

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:03.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be right back
with more from Jimmy Fallon.

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:04.784 line:92%
Those are outstanding shoes.

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What are you talking --
Am I wearing shoes?

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:10.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're so good.
You might not remember this.

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:14.126
My first year on the show,
you would -- it was a time -

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:15.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were on the show
longer than me.

00:08:15.595 --> 00:08:16.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-Although this never

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:18.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
happened for me, so maybe this
had not anything

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:22.268
to do with tenure,
but people would send you shoes,

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:24.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you would have, like,
boxes of shoes.

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.138
And I remember once --
You were being very cool.

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:27.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was my first year
on the show, you're like,

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:28.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey!
You want these shoes?"

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:32.912
And they were like these orange,
furry Adidas shoes.

00:08:32.912 --> 00:08:33.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes!
Oh, I remember that!

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:35.781
-You remember them, right?
They're the ugliest shoes

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:37.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the world, but I was --
I just assumed,

00:08:37.984 --> 00:08:40.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you gave them to me,
they were cool shoes.

00:08:40.052 --> 00:08:42.588
And I remember wearing the
to see my college friends.

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:44.023
I had basically been on the show
for three months,

00:08:44.023 --> 00:08:46.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just, like,
walked into a Chicago bar,

00:08:46.225 --> 00:08:49.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were like, "No!"
-"What the heck?!

00:08:49.328 --> 00:08:51.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
He gave them to you
for a reason!

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:53.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
You shouldn't wear -- no one
should wear those shoes!"

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
They look like Muppets.

00:08:55.401 --> 00:08:57.904
-Yeah, they were Muppets.
-They were fuzzy shoes.

00:08:57.904 --> 00:08:59.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they were real bad.
-They were awful.

00:08:59.105 --> 00:09:02.842
-And it was an act -- I'd like
to believe it was an act of --

00:09:02.842 --> 00:09:04.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were testing me,
and I failed.

00:09:04.477 --> 00:09:05.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember,
everything I got sent,

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:07.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to wear,
'cause it's free clothes.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I go, "This is amazing."
And I think --

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:12.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to say Hugo Boss
sent me a jacket.

00:09:12.451 --> 00:09:13.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was one of the first things
I got.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:16.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was silver.
Like, metal silver.

00:09:16.789 --> 00:09:18.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like aluminum foil.
-Right.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.726
-And I go, "This is --
I guess I can wear this?"

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:26.198
And I went to a bar
over on 9th Avenue or something,

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:27.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
wearing this
aluminum-foil jacket

00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:31.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
at like 3:00 in the morning,
and I got mugged.

00:09:31.637 --> 00:09:32.238 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:32.238 --> 00:09:34.440
And these guys were like,
"Give me that jacket."

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Absolutely.
You got it, man."

00:09:37.343 --> 00:09:38.010 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The guy was like --

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
I almost wanted to give
it to him too fast.

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:41.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was like, "You know what?
We're cool."

00:09:41.614 --> 00:09:43.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go,
"You don't want the jacket?"

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "I don't, actually.
I go, "Okay."

00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:47.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I left -- I go, "I'm never
wearing this dumb thing --

00:09:47.687 --> 00:09:48.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A mugger --
When I wore your shoes,

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:52.024
a mugger stopped me
and gave me money for new shoes.

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:54.160 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:56.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is your fourth book.
-Unbelievable.

00:09:56.329 --> 00:10:00.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And this is the most word
in any of your books.

00:10:00.032 --> 00:10:02.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This, for me,
is a real tour de force.

00:10:02.501 --> 00:10:05.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is, like --
This is, like, my "Goldfinch."

00:10:05.504 --> 00:10:06.038 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:06.038 --> 00:10:08.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is --
This is unbelievable.

00:10:08.941 --> 00:10:10.476 line:92%
What I've done here was --

00:10:10.476 --> 00:10:12.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Finally got my money's worth
on my laptop.

00:10:12.612 --> 00:10:13.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-'Cause, like, really, I go,

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:16.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
the other books have kind of
been like text messages

00:10:16.682 --> 00:10:18.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
turned into books.
-But I will say,

00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:20.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
as someone
who has your other books,

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:21.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're wonderful
for a certain age.

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:24.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I imagine that your kids
get a little older,

00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:27.360
and then you write a book
that they will be into.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:28.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
So, this one is --

00:10:28.728 --> 00:10:30.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, what happened is
I always wanted to do

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:32.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Christmas book,
and I just couldn't think

00:10:32.865 --> 00:10:34.500 size:84% position:42%
of what the hook was
or what I wanted to do.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause I'm telling you, man,
it's the coolest vibe

00:10:37.803 --> 00:10:40.206 size:81% position:41%
when you write a book,
and it was, you know,

00:10:40.206 --> 00:10:42.575 size:88% position:44%
"Dada moo, Dada quack,"
that was the first book.

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:44.877
And then, you get these videos
of these kids reading the book

00:10:44.877 --> 00:10:48.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
with their parents back to you
and it's awesome.

00:10:48.047 --> 00:10:51.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
You start getting --
I got videos from teachers

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.919
saying, like,
"Hey, you're teaching confidence

00:10:53.919 --> 00:10:57.256
in these kids to, like, laug
and know that reading's cool,"

00:10:57.256 --> 00:10:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you go like, "Oh, my gosh.
Of course.

00:10:59.692 --> 00:11:01.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was my plan
the whole time."

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And so, you get a good buzz.

00:11:03.963 --> 00:11:06.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, I was walking Winnie
home from school one day,

00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:09.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she goes, "How many more
sleeps till we go to --"

00:11:09.769 --> 00:11:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she doesn't even
have a lisp.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.772
I just did that, because
it makes her sound cuter.

00:11:12.772 --> 00:11:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she goes --
She was so cute --

00:11:15.408 --> 00:11:17.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How many more sleeps
till we go to grandma's house?

00:11:17.843 --> 00:11:21.180
And I go --
My kid sounds like Jay Leno now.

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:23.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
My kid is --

00:11:23.683 --> 00:11:24.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ As Jay Leno ]
"How many more sleeps

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
till we, uh,
go to grandma's house?"

00:11:26.752 --> 00:11:28.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:11:28.287 --> 00:11:29.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
Dude, I get everything
from Leno.

00:11:29.288 --> 00:11:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get everything --
My kids talk like Jay Leno

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's weird, because
you're a good impressionist,

00:11:32.358 --> 00:11:34.060 size:84% position:42%
and now we're seeing
you can't do your kids.

00:11:34.060 --> 00:11:35.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very interesting.
-Can't do my kids.

00:11:35.528 --> 00:11:37.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like your blind spot
as an impressionist.

00:11:37.797 --> 00:11:40.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So she -- I go,
"How many more sleeps?"

00:11:40.199 --> 00:11:40.800 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's so cute.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:41.967 size:81% position:41%
I didn't have sleeps
when I was growing up.

00:11:41.967 --> 00:11:43.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had days -- "How many more
days until something?"

00:11:43.836 --> 00:11:46.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "Five More Sleeps
'Til Christmas" would be cute,

00:11:46.706 --> 00:11:49.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I couldn't always wait
for Santa to come.

00:11:49.408 --> 00:11:51.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was talking to my son
about Christmas

00:11:51.744 --> 00:11:53.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
and telling him
how I could never sleep

00:11:53.212 --> 00:11:56.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
the night before Christmas
And then I realized,

00:11:56.515 --> 00:11:57.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
it wasn't a helpful thing
to tell him,

00:11:57.983 --> 00:12:00.986
because I'm basically giving him
an excuse to now...

00:12:00.986 --> 00:12:03.289
-Yeah.
-...turn around on Christmas Eve

00:12:03.289 --> 00:12:05.057
and be like, "You couldn't
do it, either, old man!"

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:06.559
-Yeah.
The fun about these things, too,

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:08.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
is, like, you make it
short enough so that it counts

00:12:08.794 --> 00:12:11.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a book, but it's also
long enough, so it is a book

00:12:11.664 --> 00:12:15.067
but there's spaces in ther
so that you can go like,

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:17.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, these are toys
that he's dreaming about."

00:12:17.169 --> 00:12:18.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you go like,
"You know, when I was a kid,

00:12:18.771 --> 00:12:23.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had a dream about this toy."
You know, my favorite toy,

00:12:23.809 --> 00:12:26.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember, I was growing up
and I wanted this robot

00:12:26.746 --> 00:12:30.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
called Marzon.
It was a walking robot.

00:12:30.349 --> 00:12:31.016 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it was in --

00:12:31.016 --> 00:12:32.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just saw the commercial
for it, like...

00:12:32.118 --> 00:12:34.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ Marzon ♪♪
And I go, "Oh, I'd love that."

00:12:34.487 --> 00:12:35.855 line:92%
So I asked Santa for Marzon.

00:12:35.855 --> 00:12:37.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, basically,
what Marzon was,

00:12:37.423 --> 00:12:40.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
is an inflatable robot
that you hooked

00:12:40.259 --> 00:12:42.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
this plastic thing to the feet
and turned it on,

00:12:42.995 --> 00:12:45.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the plastic would move
the robot and whatever.

00:12:45.931 --> 00:12:51.670
And I think Santa was testin
out the eggnog the night before.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:52.204 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:12:52.204 --> 00:12:55.908
Let's just say, the plastic part
didn't come with my Marzon

00:12:55.908 --> 00:12:58.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, I got an inflatable doll
for Christmas.

00:12:58.844 --> 00:13:00.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I woke up, I go,
"Oh, my gosh!

00:13:00.579 --> 00:13:01.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
Marzon!
Santa's the best."

00:13:01.981 --> 00:13:04.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go in, and it's just
an inflatable robot.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:05.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And that's all it does.

00:13:05.618 --> 00:13:06.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't do anything.
-No walking.

00:13:06.685 --> 00:13:09.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Doesn't walk. No, that part
did not come with my toy.

00:13:09.388 --> 00:13:12.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, I mean, you tell thes
fun stories when you're readin

00:13:12.191 --> 00:13:13.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
to your kids, you're like,
"Oh, I remember.

00:13:13.726 --> 00:13:14.593 line:92%
I did this and all that stuff.

00:13:14.593 --> 00:13:20.299
And then, the spoiler at end
of this -- my M. Night Shyamalan

00:13:20.299 --> 00:13:23.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
of children's book authors
at the end is,

00:13:23.569 --> 00:13:26.639
you see that it's all abou
the buildup of getting the toys.

00:13:26.639 --> 00:13:29.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's all about the fun and
the singing and the decorating

00:13:29.708 --> 00:13:31.577 size:84% position:42%
and this type of year
and just getting to it,

00:13:31.577 --> 00:13:32.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's kind of
the point of it.

00:13:32.812 --> 00:13:35.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
The kid wants to get excited
for next Christmas.

00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:37.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which does also makes sense
because, ultimately,

00:13:37.983 --> 00:13:40.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
even if your Marzon
had the right stuff,

00:13:40.886 --> 00:13:41.754 size:88% position:44% line:92%
about an hour into it --

00:13:41.754 --> 00:13:42.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wouldn't be playing
with Marzon.

00:13:42.855 --> 00:13:47.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
My grandfather use to throw it
out of the upper window.

00:13:47.359 --> 00:13:49.862
When a school bus would come
and pick me and my sister up

00:13:49.862 --> 00:13:51.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
in front of our house,
and he would just

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:52.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
try to embarrass me
every time he could,

00:13:52.765 --> 00:13:55.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause all the kids
are on the bus, waiting for us

00:13:55.067 --> 00:13:55.935 line:92%
And we'd get on the school bus

00:13:55.935 --> 00:13:58.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he would come out
in a clown wig or something.

00:13:58.637 --> 00:13:59.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they'd be like,
"What's going on?"

00:13:59.939 --> 00:14:01.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I remember,
he threw Marzon

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:03.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
out the second-floor window,
and everyone's like,

00:14:03.542 --> 00:14:07.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What is going on?
The Fallons are so weird, man.

00:14:07.146 --> 00:14:09.915 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please be a comedian
when you grow up." Yeah.

00:14:09.915 --> 00:14:11.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congrats on the book,
my friend,

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.918 line:92%
and thanks for being here.

00:14:12.918 --> 00:14:14.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're going downstairs
to do a show now.

00:14:14.453 --> 00:14:15.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Here we go.
Yeah.

00:14:15.754 --> 00:14:19.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got to say, thanks for doing
what you're doing, man.

00:14:19.058 --> 00:14:22.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "I gotta come up
and tell you guys

00:14:22.161 --> 00:14:24.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're doing a great job,
'cause I watch you every night

00:14:24.597 --> 00:14:26.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yeah.
I really appreciate it, bud.

00:14:26.699 --> 00:14:27.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're awesome.
-Right back at you.

00:14:27.766 --> 00:14:30.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Best to Alexi and the kids.
-And the same to you.

00:14:30.703 --> 00:14:31.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The Tonight Show
